  "scope": "The whole original server (every Kotlin and Java file under Server/src/main, compiled unchanged with Kotlin 1.8.20 and javac on JDK 11 against the dependencies its POM names, as oracle/world-trace compiles it) booted in one JVM by the original ServerConfigParser.parse and GameWorld.prompt(false) over world-trace's world template (worldprops/default.conf with enable_bots=false). After the boot the harness reads, by reflection, four registries for the option names DoorManagingPlugin registers as scenery defaults (open, close, shut, go-through): InteractionListeners.listeners (keys of the SCENERY type, by id and catch-all), InteractionListeners.interactions (defineInteraction metadata), PluginInteractionManager.objectInteractions (by scenery id, listed under all four options because the plugin is asked whatever the option) and each loaded SceneryDefinition's handlers ('option:<name>' entries whose handler is not DoorManagingPlugin). Each row is 'id option kind class'; id -1 is a catch-all. The four comment lines name the default handler of each option. Established: which scenery id and option pairs the original registered other content for at start-up on this build. Not established: what that content does, registrations made after start-up, scenery that reaches an option through a morph (child id) and whether a listed scenery offers the option at all. Class names of Kotlin lambdas depend on the compiler version. Two fresh JVM runs must agree byte for byte before the fixture is written or accepted.",
